; The facade's command line, end to end, as a shell session — the level
; SKILL.md §5 gives argument parsing, error messages and exit codes,
; and the level windtrap's own walkthrough teaches
; (examples/x-blueprint/test/cram). [Windtrap.run] ends every branch in
; [exit], so half its contract is an exit code, which is the one thing
; cram pins natively: a bare command asserts 0, and a trailing [N]
; asserts N.
;
; suite_main is the suite under the flags — five tests, no clock and no
; network, small enough for a session to pin whole streams. The deps
; line is load-bearing: without it dune would not rebuild the fixture
; before running a session, and every .t here would exercise stale code.
;
; Not under @admit, like every other directory whose subject runs where
; no arming reaches it (see ../dune): the code these sessions are about
; executes in the child.

(executable
 (name suite_main)
 (modules suite_main)
 (libraries windtrap))

(cram
 (applies_to :whole_subtree)
 (deps suite_main.exe))
